 "title": "How to Rehearse a Job Interview with AI",
 "topic": "ai tools",
 "summary": "The creator suggests using voice-mode AI to simulate a realistic job interview and get immediate feedback. By prompting the AI to act as a hiring manager and then switching roles to a coach, candidates can practice out loud and learn where to improve.",
 "key_points": [
  "Prompt the AI to act as a sharp, slightly skeptical hiring manager for the specific role who has read your resume.",
  "Do not type your answers; turn on voice mode on your phone and talk to the AI out loud.",
  "When the interview is done, tell the AI to break character and act as your interview coach.",
  "Ask the coach to tell you where you were weak, where you fumbled, and what you should have said.",
  "Ask the coach to give you three ways you could have answered a specific question better."
 ],
 "content": "The first time you say the most important thing, you should not be in the most important room. You are the hiring manager for a senior product role. You are sharp, you're a little skeptical, and you've read my resume, so go ahead and interview me. And here's the move that makes it all real. Don't type it. Talk to it. Turn on the voice mode. On your phone. And when I'm done, I want both the agent and me to break character. Now you're my interview coach. Tell me where I was weak, where I fumbled, what I should have said. Give me three ways I could have answered that question better.",
